 "_comment": "Shared by the API's ColumnLabels tests and the UI's format.spec.ts (design D6). Each case gives the indicator's column labels (null when it has none), the widget's display (null when it has none), the widget's config (only measure and ratio matter), the indicator's label, and the expected results: `plotted` (what the widget plots, for captions) and `names` (the name shown for each listed column). The widget's label wins over the indicator's, which wins over the column's own name; a blank widget label or indicator label means none. A display may also carry a caption: its own text replaces the whole `plotted` line, and a hidden caption keeps it. Every name and value is invented.",
